        "id": 127254,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-15T12:33:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We crave fat, salt and sugar because these things were scarce in our evolutionary past and so we needed the motivation to scarf them down whenever they were available.</p><p>Unfortunately we haven't had any time to evolve out of it since, now those things are very much not scarce.</p><p>I bought a standard jar of supermarket tomato pasta sauce the other week. It was disgusting. It would have been okay if there hadn't been enough sugar in it to make me confused about whether I was eating pasta or a dessert. I think I'm losing my tolerance for sweetness as I get older (although I love desserts I hate anything too sweet) but even so, I don't know how anyone can stand to eat stuff like that.</p><p>It made it very clear to me why I usually make my own tomato sauce for pasta.</p>",
